# Monet — build-time configuration. Copy to `.env.local` for dev; set the same keys in the
# Vercel project for production. Everything here is OPTIONAL: with none of it set, Monet works
# exactly as before and GitHub access uses a personal access token (Settings → "Use a token
# instead"). Setup walkthrough: docs/GITHUB-APP.md.

# --- public, safe to ship in the bundle -----------------------------------------------------
# The GitHub App's Client ID (App settings → "Client ID", looks like Iv23li…).
VITE_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
# The App's URL slug, used for the "Repository access" links
# (https://github.com/apps/<slug>) — from the App's public page URL.
VITE_GITHUB_APP_SLUG=monet
# Only needed if the token exchange is not served from this origin (e.g. `npm run dev` talking
# to the deployed function). Defaults to /api/github/token.
# VITE_GITHUB_TOKEN_ENDPOINT=https://monet.mouftools.com/api/github/token

# --- server side: set in Vercel only, NEVER in a VITE_ variable ------------------------------
# A VITE_ prefix would inline it into the client bundle. These are read by api/github/token.ts.
# GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
# GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=
